From b5bce69413d26c28f3ff8b4dce4e9c1b20b66e0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:39:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the Monitor setting shows each display by its
 name

The setting listed the outputs by the names of their connectors ("HDMI-A-2",
"DP-2"), and nothing on the screen told which display was which: with a TV and
two monitors on one card, the way to know was to unplug the others.

Each connected output is now shown by the name that its display gives itself
in its EDID, with the connector after it ("LG TV SSCR2 (HDMI-A-2)"), and with
its graphics device where the outputs offered are on more than one ("Odyssey
G60SD (DP-2, NVIDIA)"). The name is the text of the display product name
descriptor of the base block (EdidDisplayName()), the text that libdisplay-info
reads for the model of a display. It is read on its own: the parser of
libdisplay-info writes its warnings about an EDID to the log each time it reads
one, and the settings list the monitors each time they are shown. An output
whose display gives no name is shown by its connector, as before.

What the setting keeps when one is chosen does not change
(OfferedOutputNames()): a choice saved before still names its output, and Kodi
starts on it as before. Default is shown in the language of the user (Kodi's
#571), and a monitor that the setting names and that is not among the
connected outputs says so ("HDMI-A-3 (not connected)").

Host test of DRMOutputChoice.h: the names of synthetic EDIDs and of the EDIDs
of four real displays, the labels, and the names kept, as before, in 1296 sets
of outputs on two devices.
